**Dmytro Starosud ([@dima-starosud](https://github.com/dima-starosud)) wrote:**

@zzzeek Thanks for confirmation!

So I don't have to call `configure_mappers()` each time I've added new `descriptor`?

**Dmytro Starosud ([@dima-starosud](https://github.com/dima-starosud)) wrote:**

@zzzeek Right, using internal API:

    from sqlalchemy.orm.mapper import _mapper_registry
    from sqlalchemy.orm.mapper import _memoized_configured_property
    for mapper in list(_mapper_registry):
        _memoized_configured_property.expire_instance(mapper)
